## 3. Kafka to Snowflake connection

Authentication uses an RSA key pair (key-pair login), not a password.

- The key pair was generated locally with openssl.
- The **public key** is registered in Snowflake on KAFKA_USER
  (`ALTER USER KAFKA_USER SET RSA_PUBLIC_KEY = '<public key>';`).
- The **private key** was shared privately with Shrawani only. It is
  used in her connector config as `snowflake.private.key`.
- Keys are stored outside this repo and are never committed.

Connector settings (no secrets):

```properties
snowflake.url.name=TJBRGSZ-RX49654.snowflakecomputing.com:443
snowflake.user.name=KAFKA_USER
snowflake.role.name=KAFKA_CONNECTOR_ROLE
snowflake.database.name=ATMOSYNC_DB
snowflake.schema.name=RAW
snowflake.topic2table.map=<kafka_topic>:IOT_SENSOR_RAW
```

